WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.010 --> 00:00:08.560
In Marvel Studios'
Ant-Man and the Wasp:

00:00:08.560 --> 00:00:12.340
Quantumania we get a close
look at the MCU's next big bad,

00:00:12.340 --> 00:00:13.450
Kang the Conqueror.

00:00:13.450 --> 00:00:15.070
And to help us break
down the design

00:00:15.070 --> 00:00:17.230
behind this
multiversal miscreant,

00:00:17.230 --> 00:00:19.480
I'm here with the director
of visual development

00:00:19.480 --> 00:00:22.090
at Marvel Studios,
Andy Park, and concept

00:00:22.090 --> 00:00:23.870
artist Constantine Sekeris.

00:00:23.870 --> 00:00:24.740
Hi, guys.
- Hi.

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:25.540
Hi.

00:00:25.540 --> 00:00:26.845
Let's dive in.

00:00:26.845 --> 00:00:28.810
Kang is such an
iconic character,

00:00:28.810 --> 00:00:31.810
and fans have been eagerly
awaiting his big screen debut.

00:00:31.810 --> 00:00:34.960
So tell us where you started
with developing the conqueror

00:00:34.960 --> 00:00:36.550
variant of this character?

00:00:36.550 --> 00:00:39.580
Whenever we're tackling any
particular villain, when we're

00:00:39.580 --> 00:00:42.250
trying to translate
comic into the MCU,

00:00:42.250 --> 00:00:45.460
we always do a deep dive into
the comic books, of course,

00:00:45.460 --> 00:00:47.470
starting off with Jack Kirby.

00:00:47.470 --> 00:00:50.650
CONSTANTINE SEKERIS: Jack Kirby
just had this design sense

00:00:50.650 --> 00:00:52.630
of just making
characters look iconic,

00:00:52.630 --> 00:00:54.490
just very simple and bold.

00:00:54.490 --> 00:00:57.670
ANDY PARK: So this is our chance
to come up with a classic look

00:00:57.670 --> 00:00:58.900
that we see from the comic.

00:00:58.900 --> 00:01:03.340
The purples, the greens,
the helmet, the blue visage.

00:01:03.340 --> 00:01:05.500
One of the very
first inspiration

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:07.840
images that was given
to me was of Kang

00:01:07.840 --> 00:01:09.940
just sitting on his throne.

00:01:09.940 --> 00:01:12.640
He's called Kang the
Conqueror for a reason.

00:01:12.640 --> 00:01:15.970
There's a certain status
that you see in him.

00:01:15.970 --> 00:01:17.200
That's where we started.

00:01:17.200 --> 00:01:20.200
The challenge in bringing
these classic comic book

00:01:20.200 --> 00:01:23.740
costumes and looks into
the MCU is we're always

00:01:23.740 --> 00:01:25.330
trying to bring a reality.

00:01:25.330 --> 00:01:29.890
So with Kang, it was bringing
in the high-tech, futuristic

00:01:29.890 --> 00:01:31.690
elements into his costume.

00:01:31.690 --> 00:01:34.240
A big part of it was his helmet.

00:01:34.240 --> 00:01:37.060
This helmet is really
unique from others we've seen.

00:01:37.060 --> 00:01:38.740
Was there a certain
functionality

00:01:38.740 --> 00:01:40.360
you needed to hit
with the design?

00:01:40.360 --> 00:01:42.040
Whenever we
design helmets, it's

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:45.277
always such an important
element to the costume.

00:01:45.277 --> 00:01:46.510
Because at the end
of the day, that's

00:01:46.510 --> 00:01:47.650
what we're looking at, right?

00:01:47.650 --> 00:01:50.410
In the original
Jack Kirby design,

00:01:50.410 --> 00:01:53.590
he's got more of like
a sort of like toaster

00:01:53.590 --> 00:01:56.230
square helmet that
started to become

00:01:56.230 --> 00:02:00.160
a little bit not as functional.

00:02:00.160 --> 00:02:05.320
We had played with adding a
clear face shield that allowed

00:02:05.320 --> 00:02:08.919
then the actor to not
have something on his face

00:02:08.919 --> 00:02:10.360
or cover up his face.

00:02:10.360 --> 00:02:14.110
It was very important for Peyton
and the leadership of Marvel

00:02:14.110 --> 00:02:16.390
to not lose his performance.

00:02:16.390 --> 00:02:20.050
And even the question of,
will his face be blue,

00:02:20.050 --> 00:02:21.820
or will it just be
Jonathan Majors?

00:02:21.820 --> 00:02:25.750
We explored both, everything
from having blue lights emit

00:02:25.750 --> 00:02:28.900
from the sides of the
helmet in towards the face,

00:02:28.900 --> 00:02:32.050
projecting and giving
him a blue tinge,

00:02:32.050 --> 00:02:37.240
to more the high-tech elements
of maybe kind of an energy

00:02:37.240 --> 00:02:39.850
shield that kind of
conforms to the face

00:02:39.850 --> 00:02:41.230
that gives him the blue look.

00:02:41.230 --> 00:02:43.330
We explored a lot
of different textures,

00:02:43.330 --> 00:02:45.430
different hues of blues.

00:02:45.430 --> 00:02:48.130
In the end, it was like,
how much can we still see

00:02:48.130 --> 00:02:51.400
Jonathan Majors' face
without seeing the sort

00:02:51.400 --> 00:02:53.560
of like blue face shield.

00:02:53.560 --> 00:02:58.270
So in the end, it was just
something very simple.

00:02:58.270 --> 00:03:00.370
Simple, but so very effective.

00:03:00.370 --> 00:03:02.740
Now what other details
did you focus on

00:03:02.740 --> 00:03:05.770
to help craft the narrative
of Kang's backstory?

00:03:05.770 --> 00:03:08.420
Yeah, the look that we were
going for is more the conqueror

00:03:08.420 --> 00:03:09.220
Kang.

00:03:09.220 --> 00:03:13.270
So he really has, like, this
regal kind of quality to him

00:03:13.270 --> 00:03:17.320
with the cave, the robes that
hearken back to conquerors

00:03:17.320 --> 00:03:18.970
of the past in human history.

00:03:18.970 --> 00:03:23.470
But then we also wanted to
infuse suggestions of, this is

00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:26.890
a Kang from the
future that has access

00:03:26.890 --> 00:03:31.030
and developed high weaponry,
high sophisticated technology.

00:03:31.030 --> 00:03:33.330
Even the way we
designed the cape

00:03:33.330 --> 00:03:35.470
is a little different
than just a normal cape

00:03:35.470 --> 00:03:36.730
as it's segmented.

00:03:36.730 --> 00:03:41.170
So bringing the technology along
with the kind of more grounded,

00:03:41.170 --> 00:03:42.490
rogue type of feel.

00:03:42.490 --> 00:03:45.550
He's got this motif on his
face, these sort of like,

00:03:45.550 --> 00:03:48.010
lines that is very iconic.

00:03:48.010 --> 00:03:50.590
And so in the fabrics,
you see that a lot

00:03:50.590 --> 00:03:53.500
with some of these
lines and textures that

00:03:53.500 --> 00:03:55.900
give strength to the character.

00:03:55.900 --> 00:03:58.060
Can you tell us more
about the design decisions

00:03:58.060 --> 00:03:59.560
behind the lines on his face?

00:03:59.560 --> 00:04:02.350
In this respect,
you have two sort

00:04:02.350 --> 00:04:05.080
of like vertical
line designs, meaning

00:04:05.080 --> 00:04:07.300
he's got the scars on his face.

00:04:07.300 --> 00:04:11.320
And then when you do see him
with a sort of like blue face

00:04:11.320 --> 00:04:13.740
guard, you've got tech lines.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:15.340
ANDY PARK: A lot of
different kind of patterning

00:04:15.340 --> 00:04:17.410
was done by the
different artists.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:20.079
And then at the end of the
day, once we got that approved,

00:04:20.079 --> 00:04:23.830
the makeup department led
by Alina Arroyo played

00:04:23.830 --> 00:04:26.050
with the ideas of
doing different scars

00:04:26.050 --> 00:04:28.030
on Jonathan Majors' face.

00:04:28.030 --> 00:04:30.040
And it also alludes
to why he has

00:04:30.040 --> 00:04:33.430
the lines in that blue
energy kind of mask.

00:04:33.430 --> 00:04:35.470
But there's a story that maybe--

00:04:35.470 --> 00:04:38.200
maybe we'll find out,
and maybe we won't.

00:04:38.200 --> 00:04:40.330
We love a good cliffhanger.

00:04:40.330 --> 00:04:43.600
Now your team has brought
such an awesome look for Kang.

00:04:43.600 --> 00:04:46.540
What are you most proud of when
looking back at the process?

00:04:46.540 --> 00:04:51.910
I'm very proud of how
the design looks on paper,

00:04:51.910 --> 00:04:54.340
and then also how
it was translated.

00:04:54.340 --> 00:04:56.530
So I'm going to have
to also give kudos

00:04:56.530 --> 00:04:59.740
to the costume
department and props

00:04:59.740 --> 00:05:04.460
for translating this
character in the real world.

00:05:04.460 --> 00:05:07.130
I'm most proud of
my team of artists

00:05:07.130 --> 00:05:11.720
and seeing that Kang was
pretty darn comic accurate,

00:05:11.720 --> 00:05:14.450
I feel like this is a Kang
that I've been wanting to see,

00:05:14.450 --> 00:05:15.980
the fans have been
wanting to see.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:19.640
We stayed as true as we
could to the comic source.

00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:22.250
Hopefully, we're not
letting any fans down.

00:05:22.250 --> 00:05:24.260
I think it looks amazing.

00:05:24.260 --> 00:05:27.200
Every time I see it, it
puts a smile on my face.

00:05:27.200 --> 00:05:28.310
We're all smiling too.

00:05:28.310 --> 00:05:29.360
Well, except for Kang.

00:05:29.360 --> 00:05:30.170
He's not a smiler.

00:05:30.170 --> 00:05:31.580
He's a conqueror.

00:05:31.580 --> 00:05:32.420
Never mind.

00:05:32.420 --> 00:05:34.460
Well, listen, Andy,
Constantine, thank you

00:05:34.460 --> 00:05:35.750
so much for chatting with us.

00:05:35.750 --> 00:05:36.620
Thanks, Langston.

00:05:36.620 --> 00:05:37.430
Thank you.

00:05:37.430 --> 00:05:40.040
And of course,
everyone, go experience

00:05:40.040 --> 00:05:42.080
Marvel Studios'
Ant-Man and the Wasp:

00:05:42.080 --> 00:05:45.370
Quantumania in theaters now.

